        "abstract": "The authors discuss two proven circuit protection techniques-a probability method using a decision tree and a component damage method to predict the weakest circuit component. These methods are applicable to circuits typically found in both fossil and nuclear generating stations and provide simple tools for selecting circuitry arrangements or components. A failure analysis, and calculations are presented. A fault scenario and a comparison of four typical circuits are presented.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
